I've written the plan for Day 251: two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The planned commit didn't happen because session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The harness command ends in || true, which suggests that's expected, but the files are only on disk, not committed.

Task 1 — Part of #1012: price `/cost` through yoagent first, then delete the yoyo rows it hides (product)
• @yuanhao decided on Nov 3 to delete yoyo's own price table and use yoagent's prices. No commits have landed on #1012 since.
• Step 1: model_pricing_with checks yoagent's price table first, after user overrides and before yoyo's own rows.
  • yoagent looks prices up by (provider, id) and yoyo by id only, so the plan matches on the id after the router prefix (like anthropic/) is stripped. If two providers price the same id differently, it falls back to yoyo's row.
  • Tests read yoagent's numbers from its built-in table rather than typing them in. Every pinned price test that goes red gets listed on #1012, with an upstream issue where yoagent looks wrong.
• Step 2: delete every yoyo row that yoagent now hides, and add a test that fails if such a row ever comes back.
• yoagent's built-in snapshot covers only about 40 models. Deleting all of yoyo's rows now would leave roughly 70 models unpriced until a live models.dev price cache is added. So the rest of the table waits for that slice, and the commit has to say why in those words.

Task 2 — Fixes #1143: GIF only where the provider accepts it (product; this is the slot for closing an old issue, since 13 are open)
• GIF stays accepted on Anthropic and Bedrock. On other providers it's refused with a reason, using the provider yoyo already records at startup (configured_provider()). If no provider is recorded, GIF is still accepted, as today.
• I found a second bug while planning: the --image error at src/cli.rs:2737 still lists "bmp" as supported. It will now build the list from the same constant the code checks against.

Done with `gh`, no files changed:
• I put the owner's decision and the three-slice scope at the top of #1012's body. The planner only sees the first 500 characters of an issue body, and before this edit those were the Oct 11 audit numbers. The original body is kept below the new scope.

